import ../../helpers/driver.dl
window queued tabs:
    ribbon "Tabs" at 0 0 sized 600 by 168:
        tab "A":
            ribbon group "First":
                tool "One" with icon "copy"
        tab "B":
            ribbon group "Second":
                tool "Two" with icon "paste"
        tab "C":
            ribbon group "Third":
                tool "Three" with icon "cut"
set state to 0
set instance to an instance of queued tabs with state (the address of state)
set view to a UI view of (the address of instance) sized 800 by 480 using font "regular" with the test UI driver
ignore update UI view (the address of view)
queue UI input of kind 3 key 258 at 0.0 0.0 with modifiers 0 containing "" in (the address of view)
set index to 0
loop while index < 4:
    queue UI input of kind 3 key 262 at 0.0 0.0 with modifiers 0 containing "" in (the address of view)
    queue UI input of kind 6 key 262 at 0.0 0.0 with modifiers 0 containing "" in (the address of view)
    increment index
ignore update UI view (the address of view)
require condition ((the value of "Tabs" in (the address of instance)) = 1) reporting "Queued arrows used focus from the previous paint"
require condition (view's focused's node's text = "B") reporting "Focus did not follow the selected tab"
queue UI input of kind 3 key 258 at 0.0 0.0 with modifiers 0 containing "" in (the address of view)
queue UI input of kind 3 key 257 at 0.0 0.0 with modifiers 0 containing "" in (the address of view)
ignore update UI view (the address of view)
require condition ((the value of "Tabs" in (the address of instance)) = 2) reporting "Queued Tab/Enter activated the previous control"
queue UI input of kind 3 key 258 at 0.0 0.0 with modifiers 1 containing "" in (the address of view)
ignore update UI view (the address of view)
require condition (view's focused's node's text = "B") reporting "Shift-Tab did not move focus backward"
close the address of view
close the address of instance
print line "Keyboard focus updates between queued events without a paint."
